  "body": "## What happens now\nA setup has no work-coordinate-system choice. The multi-setup plumbing is in\nplace (several setups per model, an active setup), but every setup generates\nand posts against the global setup origin - the world/G54 zero. There is no\nway to say \"this setup is machined at G55\": stock-top, safe/retract/plane\nheights and depths all stay computed about the global origin, so a second\nfixture or a re-sent work at a shifted zero cannot be set up without moving\nthe model geometry or hand-editing the NC.\n\n## Expected\nA \"Work coordinate\" picker on the setup (G54 - G59, default G54) that makes\nthe chosen system real:\n- heights and planes (stock top, clearance/retract, top/bottom of cut) are\n  taken relative to the selected work coordinate, not the global origin, for\n  every operation in the setup;\n- verify/simulation use the same correction so verdicts match the machine\n  position the toolpath will run at;\n- posts emit the chosen offset in the program preamble (G54..G59) so the NC\n  tells the controller which system the numbers belong to.\n\n## Notes\n- User request 2026-11-08: \"the code is prepared for multisetups as of now we\n  only need to be able to pick a different work coordinate so heights and\n  planes get corrected\" - the setup-multiplicity work itself is done; this is\n  only the WCS choice and its corrections.\n- The change must go through a command (Everything Is a Command): an\n  undoable ChangeWorkOffset on the setup, like the other setup edits.\n- Related: #181 (setting offsets via the MCP server only), #51 (Heidenhain\n  preset selection for other work offsets).\n\n## Done means\n- The setup property panel shows the picker; the value round-trips through\n  save/load and undo/redo.\n- A G55 setup posts the G55 word in its preamble and its planes/heights read\n  against that zero; a pinning test (two setups, same op, different offsets)\n  proves the coordinates differ by exactly the offset and nothing else.\n",
